{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1551902-any-alternative-ideas-on-arcanoi-and-lore","id":1551902,"title":"Any alternative ideas on Arcanoi and Lore?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-28T19:16:37-07:00","id":1551902,"title":"Any alternative ideas on Arcanoi and Lore?","content":"Demon the Fallen &amp; Wraith the Oblivion are among my favorite lines in the WoD, however I don't really like the way their powers work. I always liked how in CofD 2e, each of the different splats powers worked and function differently. So I wanted to know if anyone has or made up their own systems for these powers.<br /> <br /> In the case of Demon specifically, I feel like its to constrained and limited for what meant to be the remnants of phemonmenal divine power, that and inconsistency of High-Torment effects, like for something that I think is primarily meant to be a temptation, I can fathom why some effects are pure drawbacks and backfires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T01:43:41-07:00","id":1551910,"title":"","content":"Demon is a strange one when it comes to Lores; they are limited and weak and the Torment versions are sometimes worse<br /> But on the other hand...? I think this is part of the theme<br /> They abandoned their &quot;jobs&quot; and were cut from the Source - they had to survive on the Faith of the Humans and when the Babel Project backfired and Humany cracked under the weight they even lost that little they had and were basically beaten in a day<br /> The Abyss &quot;Hell&quot; weakened them further and only the weakest of the weakest escaped /fit through the cracks and even those are constrained by their human hosts with the added bonus of not fully or not at all remember the past and themselves<br /> You basically have not that much to work with<br /> <br /> The two other settings that are closely tied to Demon are Vampire and Mage (or if you go with the Werewolves are distant descendants of the Malhim, that too or if you keep in mind what was on page 65, in the Chapter Three: The House of Fire and Stone section &quot;While they [the Artificers] did speak with the spirits of the stone and earth, of electron and molecule, they did not <i>create</i> those spirits. They simply allowed them to form naturally around the material. While the other Elohim worked in the spirital realms, the ethereal layers of reality, the Artificers stay in the material realm to fashion the stuff of Creation&quot; - the Angels of Fundament were aware of the existence of spirits, even were able to speak with them!) and of course Wraith but that one is situational even with the Lady of Fate was Eve and the Malfeans are the Sebettu Charon and his team that built their great fortress deep in &quot;<i>Haven</i>&quot; that became the <i>Labyrinth </i>\u200band descended into Oblivion in order to escape imprisonment at the Abyss\u200b...<br /> <br /> Vampire is obvious, Caine's act made the War bloody and destructive and his kind recieved their fair share of Curses from the Archangels, just like how Michael cursed the Sebettu.<br /> Mage is what Lucifer always wanted, to see the Humans Ascend, ignite that divine spark themselves and shape reality - Vampires with their Disciplines are the tiwsted dark mirror of that gift<br /> Both are powerful, more often than not more powerful than your avarage Sebettu and I think that is the whole deal<br /> They are Humans who one way or another could and would become powerfull while you, a Fallen Angel who sacrificed everything for Humanity live on scraps and barely able to do miracles to the point it outright can fail if enough people see and simply don't belive.<br /> Your powers don't suposed to be awesome, but weak and pathetic, shadow of its former self, echo of a glorious past you don't even fully remember and Vampires and Mages or simple humans posess what many feared deeple... and coveted jelously<br /> The Torment powers are not necesarily &quot;tempting&quot; - some of them are powerfull but only marginally at best - but the reflection of your soul warped by the Abyss, the Torment and carries the potential to cause collateral damage even if you want to help. They are not there to tempt you, more like what awaits you if you slowly let your very self errode<br /> <br /> But to answer your question, the best way to &quot;solve&quot; this power thing issue is to basically adopt the Spheres from Mage and let them work with that<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-29-2025, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T15:56:56-07:00","id":1551929,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was by design. First, because nowhere in the text is said that the powers of the Fallen work in a fundamentally different, &quot;weaker&quot; way, and second because everything indicates the Angels work under almost the exact same rules (the three distinctions being that they don't <i>necessarily</i> have Torment, they have an infinite source of temporary Faith, and they don't feel the pull of the Abyss). Everything seems to indicate that the difference between a regular Fallen and an Angel should be just in the raw number of dots.<br /> <br /> There are other possible considerations, but they cut both ways: Earthbound have extra empowering mechanics, but it isn't clear if they're something Angels had before. It isn't clear if the Generals of Lucifer use the same rules as other Earthbound or not, it isn't clear if they're weaker or stronger than the average Angel, or even than the top dogs of the Angelic Hosts. Lucifer himself appears a bunch of times (more than any other Highest-End monster in the WoD) and seems to follow the same rules as everyone, but maybe not, and he didn't suffered most of the things that could have weakened other Fallen.<br /> <br /> All things considered, while the interpretation that the Lores are weak by design is possible, I don't see real, consistent evidence. And they're not consistently weak, either, they're all over the place. Some are quite strong, and more than a few have at least one capability that is completely (or almost) out of reach to anyone else (like how by the description of the <b>Lore of Awakening</b>, objects animated by it aren't <i>just</i> animated, but effectively alive, whatever that means).<br /> <br /> What it does seem is just that the Lores are badly designed. Partly as a result from being hastily done, partly because it was the first-and-only edition of the game, so there was no feedback to inform changes. An actual design choice for them being weak would be more clearly stated and consistent.<br /> <br /> Now, this isn't necessarily terrible as far as balance goes, as laughable as trying to balance splats is within WoD. Demons have some ludicrous advantages: they're better than even Mages at finding out things and seeing through concealment, they're virtually unkillable without ST intervention and completely immune to mind/emotion control, not to say that Faith is ridiculously easy to replenish in comparison with any other supernatural fuel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T19:06:24-07:00","id":1551932,"title":"","content":"I would say my viewpoint on Lores is similar to monteparnas, in that the Lores are rather inconsistent &amp; feeling Angels &amp; Demons working under similar rules. Going back to my initial statement, I wanted to know if any has or came up with their mechcanics and systems for Lores &amp; Arcanoi that are &amp; feel different to the other splats, not just a 5 dot ladder like VtM. Like how in CofD, the closest splat powers get are Vampire's Disciplines &amp; Geist's Haunts, both being 5 dot ladders. But in Geist the intial dot creates a Haunt specific condition with later dot applying upgrades and additional options to said condition, and then their is Keys &amp; Unlockings.<br /> <br /> It was Hsienfan's <i>The Relentless Age </i>&amp; <i>In the Realm of Gods and Dreams, </i>power systems for its PCs that made me wonder if anyone else has made their own for Demon &amp; Wraith. I'd like to do it myself but I've only ever read the books so I wouldn't know how to do mechcanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1551902-any-alternative-ideas-on-arcanoi-and-lore?p=1551929#post1551929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this isn't necessarily terrible as far as balance goes, as laughable as trying to balance splats is within WoD. Demons have some ludicrous advantages: they're better than even Mages at finding out things and seeing through concealment</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? I do remember Demons having the ability to sense all supernatural stuff going on in miles wide radius, but how would they be better at gathering information in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T19:55:15-07:00","id":1551933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrere Oil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1551902-any-alternative-ideas-on-arcanoi-and-lore?p=1551932#post1551932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to my initial statement, I wanted to know if any has or came up with their mechcanics and systems for Lores &amp; Arcanoi <b>that are &amp; feel different to the other splats</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bold mine.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, nope. I can't say I've seen everything, far from that, but I did seen some discussions on this topic before. All the attempted solutions I saw stick to the 5 dot ladder system that is a staple of the WoD (even Werewolf uses it in a sense, as you still rank Gifts from 1 to 5).<br /> <br /> Most try to do one of three things: redesign the Lores within the same structure; use Mage's Sphere system, with or without tweaks; use the rules from Devil's Due and ignore DtF (they are the same beings, just not the same set of rules). None is particularly what you're looking for, although you may like DD and pick it (I personally don't like it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrere Oil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1551902-any-alternative-ideas-on-arcanoi-and-lore?p=1551932#post1551932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? I do remember Demons having the ability to sense all supernatural stuff going on in miles wide radius, but how would they be better at gathering information in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>This sense is the main reason, but not the only one. Remember, though, that it is a skill roll with information scaling to successes, so a Demon may learn a lot about the power being used. And well, they sense <i>every single power</i> in miles. Seeing through concealment adds to that, as their particular way of piercing illusions completely ignores the ability and power of their creator, and work on any kind of concealment.<br /> <br /> Add to that what they can do with their Names. While a True Name is obviously a secret to be kept, a Demon may spy on anyone that says their Celestial Name, and that's not something other denizens of the WoD are aware of. Dropping your name around is somewhat risky, but can let you witness a lot of conversations of interest. In fact, one simple move you can make is to tell a Thrall your Celestial Name (which you're probably going to do anyways for other benefits) and let them be interrogated later by your target. When the Thrall reveals the name of their master, you instantly get a VIP access to the interrogation. It isn't without risk, but being creative you can do a lot with that.<br /> <br /> You can also leverage your other abilities. You can make your Thralls better information gatherers, you can make suicidal recon missions knowing you'll come back in a new body, you can simply use the fact you're a divine being (albeit a Fallen one) to convince people to tell you things, even to convince them that you already know anything you need. This isn't something only Demons can do, but in <i>my experience</i> it is generally easier to talk your way through getting good info when you're a Demon, even if you're just talking BS.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I forgot to mention early: Thralls are possibly the most useful and easy to make kind of &quot;Supernatural Retainer&quot; in WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T07:35:15-07:00","id":1551942,"title":"","content":"I experimented with an alternative power system for Wraith. A while back there was a discussion about whether Arcanoi count as magic/sorcery which somehow led to speculation about Dark Ages Wraith and in that context, how Arcanoi would look like before the formalization (and honestly, gatekeeping) by the Guilds.<br /> <br /> The TLDR of the discussion is that Arcanoi are more like Abilities that extend mundane Talents and Skills to the metaphysics that Wraiths operate in - it's more like learning to drive a car than channeling mystic energy to wrap reality.<br /> <br /> I tried to capture that idea with a more dynamic, less linear Arcanoi system.<br /> <br /> You get an additional stat block that are basically keywords for Wraith specific Knowledge: Shadow, Psyche, Fetters, Passion, Pathos, Corpus, Tempest, Fate etc.<br /> <br /> You get dots 1-5 as usual, with each level representing the extent of what you can do with these things: <br /> 1. Perceive/Evaluate<br /> 2. Manipulation (self)<br /> 3. Manipulation (other)<br /> 4. Mend/Damage<br /> 5. Transform/Enable/Disable<br /> <br /> 1 Pathos cost per level<br /> Roll Attribute + Ability<br /> <br /> For example, if you wanted to shape the Corpus of another Wraith you would need Corpus 3 and do a Dex + Craft roll.<br /> <br /> I never fleshed this out. You run into unclear use cases a lot and there would probably be many situations in which the descriptors of the power levels don't fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T07:45:59-07:00","id":1551943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1551902-any-alternative-ideas-on-arcanoi-and-lore?p=1551929#post1551929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it was by design. First, because nowhere in the text is said that the powers of the Fallen work in a fundamentally different, &quot;weaker&quot; way,.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest it is murky at best<br /> <br /> <b>Core - P.90</b> &quot;Each House has different visages that alter the shape of our mortal bodies. It's a shadow of our true form, before God stripped away much of our being.&quot;<br /> <b>Core - P.169</b> &quot;God declared the covenant with the Fallen to be forever broken and denied them the power of His blessing, thus reducing the rebels to mere shadows of their former selves.God's curse rendered the Fallen impotent, unable to work their will upon the cosmos.&quot; (\u2026) &quot;Where the Fallen once roamed the earth as radiant spirits, they must now anchor themselves in human flesh, at best a difficult and desperate situation.&quot;<br /> <b>Houses of the Fallen</b> - p.103 &quot;Ahrimal quickly appreciated that the Fallen were mare shadows of their former sleves and in no condition to survive if soemone lanched a coordinated assault&quot;<br /> <br /> While not a Demon supplement (or more or less it is...) <br /> <b>Devil's Due</b> - p.20 &quot;Powerless and alone, the demons would be left for all time to contemplate their sins and pay the price for their crimes. Stripping the rebels of almost all their power, God withdrew again, and His Host banished the demon forces into Hell.&quot;<br /> <br /> But you are right, it is more like implied they are weaker post-Abyss / Post-Fall and I interpret it that way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T10:52:19-07:00","id":1551948,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the book doesn't give us any info on <i>how</i> this difference in power is. Your interpretation is valid, I just don't see it as <i>intentional</i>.<br /> <br /> I really wish we could have had a Demon 20 edition. And as much as I fear a D5, it would be better than the decades of nothing we have. Changeling got a lot of improvement from 1st to 2nd edition, and even more in C20. I'd love to see Demon developed beyond what was, in the end, more a draft than a finished product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T15:03:17-07:00","id":1551981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1551902-any-alternative-ideas-on-arcanoi-and-lore?p=1551933#post1551933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the attempted solutions I saw stick to the 5 dot ladder system that is a staple of the WoD (even Werewolf uses it in a sense, as you still rank Gifts from 1 to 5).</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify myself it's not the 5 dot ladder approach I necesarily have an issue with, it more due to the only differences Lores have with VtM's Disciplines being their High-Torment effects. Whereas in my previous example with CofD, Geist's Haunts are differentiated by Haunt Conditions &amp; Keys.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T17:25:17-07:00","id":1551983,"title":"","content":"Yes, the answer stands.<br /> <br /> Basically, those attempts at correcting Lores don't change the basic mechanics too much, they're still Disciplines with added Torment versions.<br /> <br /> Gifts are the powers mechanic that's most unique in the whole WoD, and it isn't by that much, and the attempts at correcting DtF that I saw don't deviate by much from this.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that in CoD even VtR changed assumptions in 2nd Edition, as the difference between Discipline levels stopped being potency/usefulness, so every level is still a potent power by itself. That's the principle behind WoD's rules that CoD abandoned: to distribute powers through 5 ranks based on how powerful they are. This principle holds true even for Gifts. But yeah, those attempts didn't even deviate that much, they just reworked the Lore's powers for whatever the author thought to be more balanced than the book's version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}